# Mounted over /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf to neutralise the welcome page
# the nginx image ships.
#
# That file declares `server_name localhost` on port 80 and sorts BEFORE
# odoo.conf, so nginx used it as the default server: any request that arrived
# by IP address instead of the configured name got the welcome page, and
# /web/login returned 404. The Odoo vhost now also claims default_server,
# which is the real fix; this removes the ambiguity entirely.
